WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.863
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Writing Skills.

2
00:00:05.163 --> 00:00:08.677
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.977 --> 00:00:14.299
Unit two: Linking Words. Today you will join ideas with and, but, because and so.

4
00:00:14.599 --> 00:00:17.368
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.333 --> 00:00:21.497
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:23.072
Link.

7
00:00:24.083 --> 00:00:26.408
Link means to join two ideas.

8
00:00:27.017 --> 00:00:28.680
Link your ideas clearly.

9
00:00:29.283 --> 00:00:32.005
Your turn. Say: Link.

10
00:00:34.867 --> 00:00:35.543
Link.

11
00:00:36.283 --> 00:00:37.250
Because.

12
00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:40.331
Because means used to give a reason.

13
00:00:40.917 --> 00:00:42.754
I study because I want a job.

14
00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:46.072
Your turn. Say: Because.

15
00:00:48.933 --> 00:00:49.946
Because.

16
00:00:50.683 --> 00:00:51.290
But.

17
00:00:52.283 --> 00:00:54.248
But means used to show a difference.

18
00:00:54.850 --> 00:00:56.397
It is cheap but good.

19
00:00:56.983 --> 00:00:58.927
Your turn. Say: But.

20
00:01:01.767 --> 00:01:02.385
But.

21
00:01:03.150 --> 00:01:03.872
So.

22
00:01:04.883 --> 00:01:07.162
So means used to show a result.

23
00:01:07.750 --> 00:01:09.657
I was tired, so I slept.

24
00:01:10.250 --> 00:01:12.345
Your turn. Say: So.

25
00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:16.120
So.

26
00:01:16.883 --> 00:01:17.873
Also.

27
00:01:18.883 --> 00:01:20.569
Also means in addition.

28
00:01:21.183 --> 00:01:22.881
She also speaks French.

29
00:01:23.483 --> 00:01:26.101
Your turn. Say: Also.

30
00:01:28.967 --> 00:01:29.852
Also.

31
00:01:30.617 --> 00:01:31.560
However.

32
00:01:32.550 --> 00:01:34.805
However means used to show contrast.

33
00:01:35.417 --> 00:01:36.812
However, it was late.

34
00:01:37.417 --> 00:01:39.558
Your turn. Say: However.

35
00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:43.169
However.

36
00:01:43.917 --> 00:01:44.697
Reason.

37
00:01:45.683 --> 00:01:47.776
Reason means why something happens.

38
00:01:48.383 --> 00:01:50.162
Give a reason for your idea.

39
00:01:50.750 --> 00:01:52.950
Your turn. Say: Reason.

40
00:01:55.800 --> 00:01:56.546
Reason.

41
00:01:57.283 --> 00:01:58.168
Result.

42
00:01:59.183 --> 00:02:01.438
Result means what happens after something.

43
00:02:02.050 --> 00:02:03.388
The result was good.

44
00:02:03.983 --> 00:02:06.787
Your turn. Say: Result.

45
00:02:09.633 --> 00:02:10.507
Result.

46
00:02:11.300 --> 00:02:15.195
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:16.050 --> 00:02:18.723
Visal, my sentences sound short and separate.

48
00:02:19.817 --> 00:02:27.856
Use linking words to join them. Use and to add, but to contrast, because for a reason and so for a result.

49
00:02:28.950 --> 00:02:30.369
Can you give an example?

50
00:02:31.483 --> 00:02:41.209
I was tired, so I went to bed early. I wanted to study, but I had no time. Notice the comma before so and but.

51
00:02:42.317 --> 00:02:43.736
What about however?

52
00:02:44.850 --> 00:02:51.162
However starts a new sentence with a comma after it. It is more formal than but. Use it in essays.

53
00:02:52.300 --> 00:02:54.021
Part three: grammar.

54
00:02:54.883 --> 00:02:57.220
Grammar focus: Linking words.

55
00:02:57.520 --> 00:02:58.695
Look at the pattern.

56
00:02:59.383 --> 00:03:01.441
I was tired, so I went to bed early.

57
00:03:02.350 --> 00:03:04.965
She studied hard because she wanted a scholarship.

58
00:03:05.900 --> 00:03:12.212
Use because for a reason and so for a result. Use but for contrast. Put a comma before so and but.

59
00:03:12.950 --> 00:03:16.694
Be careful! Don't say: I was tired because I slept.

60
00:03:18.633 --> 00:03:21.190
Say: I was tired, so I slept.

61
00:03:21.490 --> 00:03:23.060
Use so for a result.

62
00:03:23.867 --> 00:03:26.531
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:27.333 --> 00:03:28.787
Reasons and Results.

64
00:03:29.087 --> 00:03:31.052
Vanna wanted to improve her writing.

65
00:03:32.067 --> 00:03:35.041
She read many examples because she needed ideas.

66
00:03:36.033 --> 00:03:38.637
She also practised every day, but it was hard.

67
00:03:39.633 --> 00:03:42.179
However, her teacher praised her progress.

68
00:03:43.167 --> 00:03:45.340
She felt happy, so she kept writing.

69
00:03:46.433 --> 00:03:50.540
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:03:51.383 --> 00:03:52.791
Because gives a blank.

71
00:03:53.091 --> 00:03:56.361
A, place. B, name. C, reason.

72
00:03:59.900 --> 00:04:01.691
The answer is C: reason.

73
00:04:02.850 --> 00:04:04.107
So shows a blank.

74
00:04:04.407 --> 00:04:07.619
A, result. B, date. C, colour.

75
00:04:11.167 --> 00:04:13.143
The answer is A: result.

76
00:04:14.283 --> 00:04:15.726
But shows a blank.

77
00:04:16.026 --> 00:04:19.563
A, number. B, contrast. C, list.

78
00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:25.332
The answer is B: contrast.

79
00:04:26.483 --> 00:04:28.146
However starts a new blank.

80
00:04:28.446 --> 00:04:31.809
A, book. B, class. C, sentence.

81
00:04:35.367 --> 00:04:37.331
The answer is C: sentence.

82
00:04:38.483 --> 00:04:40.982
Vanna read examples because she needed blank.

83
00:04:41.282 --> 00:04:44.483
A, ideas. B, money. C, sleep.

84
00:04:48.033 --> 00:04:50.428
The answer is A: ideas.

85
00:04:51.633 --> 00:04:54.611
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:04:55.450 --> 00:04:57.299
Which linking words do you use?

87
00:05:06.083 --> 00:05:07.781
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:08.081 --> 00:05:24.238
I use and to add ideas, but to show contrast, because to give a reason and so to show a result. In formal writing I use however. Linking words make my writing smooth.

89
00:05:24.538 --> 00:05:26.387
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:27.283 --> 00:05:31.282
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and linking words.

91
00:05:31.582 --> 00:05:35.860
Today's value is communication. Speak clearly and listen carefully.

92
00:05:36.160 --> 00:05:38.720
See you in Unit three. Goodbye!

93
00:05:39.020 --> 00:05:41.695
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

